acceptance_criteria: Versioned evidence-backed disjoint partition declarations with immutable operand and declaration pins; Explicit reviewed addition preserves union population source evidence uncertainty and unknowns while incompatible contexts refuse before writes; Real no-git SDK trackers verify native CAS process concurrency crash replay backward reads and behavioral revert proofs; README and ARCHITECTURE document a pinned public tracker example and scoped limits
parent: pm-unit-release
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T20:18:14.828Z",codex-astra,"Scope: deliver versioned evidence-backed disjoint partition declarations, native CAS/replay, immutable operand and declaration pins, and safe exact addition. Preserve existing version-1 records. General compatibility mappings, product/division/exponent unit AST, and weighted ratio aggregation will be separate Feature items with explicit acceptance criteria. Validate with real no-git SDK trackers, shared OS-process writers, crash/replay boundaries and isolated behavioral reverts."
  "2026-11-06T20:20:27.213Z",codex-astra,"Split remaining original scope into pm-unit-compatibility, pm-unit-unit-ast and pm-unit-weighted-ratios. New declarations upgrade only their owner to state version 2; version-1 reads and exact-context derivations remain unchanged. Review attribution is submitted evidence, not authenticated approval or a proof of real-world disjointness."
  "2026-11-06T20:26:41.155Z",codex-astra,"Focused declaration suite: 10/10 passed using real SDK trackers. Independent OS callers raced at before_update: exactly one committed and the other received revision_conflict; explicit re-review preserved both declarations. SIGKILL before and after the durable update converged on one declaration and audit event using the original key. Public read-only tracker copy at 0578835e5d5b46aac334bb8368905deb04530b61 contains seven Features plus one Epic; pinned membership evidence reproduces eight items. Lint, docstrings and zero-duplication gates passed. Full coverage, packed consumers and isolated behavioral reverts are in progress."
  "2026-11-06T20:30:47.459Z",codex-astra,"The required pm test run completed successfully: 10 tests, 10 passed, zero failed/skipped/cancelled. Linked command includes build, test typecheck and the three declaration test files. Tracker test-result tracking is disabled by existing policy, so this comment preserves the successful result without changing tracker settings. The initial full suite passed 88/88; its coverage measurement was invalidated by a concurrent rebuild and is being rerun serially before any coverage claim."
  "2026-11-06T20:33:47.304Z",codex-astra,"Behavioral revert proofs: all 10 new safeguard removals failed in disposable emitted-code copies, covering admission, operand fingerprints, semantic boundaries, evidence capacity, immutable declaration fingerprints, CLI dispatch, cross-process native CAS, process-kill replay, union identity and transitive declaration witnesses. The linked-worktree SDK health check reports merge-driver configuration drift against the enclosing repository despite Git resolving this package correctly; no other repository was changed. Full gates will run in a standalone package clone to isolate that SDK discovery issue."
  "2026-11-06T20:34:43.506Z",codex-astra,"Opened PR #8 at commit de51442 with the implementation, tracker split, docs, public fixture and ten isolated behavioral revert proofs; the unchanged implementation also passed the revert verification. CodeRabbit review was queued immediately after opening, independently of CI. Full npm and Bun gates are running serially in a standalone package clone."
  "2026-11-06T20:39:32.133Z",codex-astra,"Self-review corrected the public-example acquisition metadata: re-acquired the same pinned public snapshot through a complete SDK read in a disposable copy and recorded its actual retrieval timestamp. The example now uses that timestamp for observation and review attribution instead of generic fixture dates, while preserving the same eight native identities and revisions. Production code is unchanged."
